practiceProblems.problemStatement:
Implement three independent capabilities from scratch:

1. Interfaces:
   - Interface Identifiable: String getId();
   - Interface Connectable: void connect(String ip);
   - Interface Recoverable: void recoverState();

2. Class NetworkNode (implements all three):
   - Field: private String nodeId
   - Constructor: NetworkNode(String id)
   - Method 1: @Override public String getId() returning nodeId
   - Method 2: @Override public void connect(String ip) printing 'Node ' + nodeId + ' established link to ' + ip
   - Method 3: @Override public void recoverState() printing 'Node ' + nodeId + ' recovered from checkpoint'

Test in Main:
NetworkNode node = new NetworkNode("NODE-TX-1");
Print 'Node ID: ' + node.getId();
node.connect("10.0.0.50");
node.recoverState();.

practiceProblems.solutionCode:
interface Identifiable {
    String getId();
}

interface Connectable {
    boolean connect(String peerIp);
}

interface Securable {
    void encryptPayload(String key);
}

class ClusterNode implements Identifiable, Connectable, Securable {
    private String nodeId;
    public ClusterNode(String nodeId) {
        this.nodeId = nodeId;
    }
    @Override
    public String getId() {
        return nodeId;
    }
    @Override
    public boolean connect(String peerIp) {
        System.out.println("Node " + nodeId + " established link to " + peerIp);
        return true;
    }
    @Override
    public void encryptPayload(String key) {
        System.out.println("Node " + nodeId + " payload secured with key " + key);
    }
}

public class ClusterApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ClusterNode node = new ClusterNode("NODE-TX-1");
        System.out.println("Node ID: " + node.getId());
        node.connect("10.0.0.1");
        node.encryptPayload("AES_KEY_88");
    }
}
